    detection: "Iron and manganese testing requires a certified laboratory water test — visual signs (staining, taste) confirm a problem exists but don't quantify severity. A combined iron/manganese panel typically costs $20–$40 from a certified lab. Testing at least once on a new well and every 3–5 years thereafter is recommended, with more frequent testing if staining or taste problems appear. Many county extension programs offer well water testing guidance and certified lab referrals. See [how to test well water](/guides/how-to-test-well-water) for step-by-step collection guidance.",
